.TH DOUBLETAKE-CTL 1 "May 2026" "doubletake" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
doubletake-ctl \- Control doubletake daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doubletake-ctl
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B doubletake-ctl
is a command-line interface for controlling the
.B doubletake
daemon. It allows you to query status, connect to and disconnect from Apple TVs,
and manage multiple simultaneous mirroring sessions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Query the status of the running doubletake daemon and list active connections
.TP
.B connect [\fITARGET\fR] [\fIPIN-OR-PASSWORD\fR]
Connect to an Apple TV, optionally supplying pairing credentials. If no target
is specified, connect to the first available discovered receiver
.TP
.B pin \fIPIN-OR-PASSWORD\fR
Submit the credential for a receiver waiting for input. The command retains its
historical name for compatibility: the pending value may be either an on-screen
PIN or a configured receiver password. Exactly one receiver must be waiting;
when multiple receivers are waiting, use
.B connect \fITARGET\fR \fIPIN-OR-PASSWORD\fR
to select one explicitly.
.TP
.B disconnect [\fITARGET\fR]
Disconnect from an Apple TV. If no target is specified, disconnects all active connections
.TP
.B reset-restore-token \fITARGET\fR
Stop one fully streaming target, clear only its saved Wayland portal restore
token, and reconnect the same IP and port. Pairing credentials and other streams
are preserved. The command refuses a target whose capture group is shared; first
disconnect the peers using that group so the old portal source can be stopped.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check daemon status:
.B doubletake-ctl status
.TP
Connect to an Apple TV:
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.77
.TP
Connect to multiple Apple TVs:
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.77
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.100
.TP
Disconnect from a specific Apple TV:
.B doubletake-ctl disconnect 192.168.1.77
.TP
Disconnect all connections:
.B doubletake-ctl disconnect
.TP
Clear one receiver's Wayland restore token and reconnect it:
.B doubletake-ctl reset-restore-token 192.168.1.77
.SH USAGE
First, start the doubletake daemon in a separate terminal or background:
.IP
.B doubletake \-daemonize
.IP
Then use
.B doubletake-ctl
to manage connections:
.IP
.B doubletake-ctl status
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.77
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.100
.PP
The JSON returned by
.B status
uses
.B needs_credential
to report pending input and
.B credential_kind
to distinguish
.B pin
from
.BR password .
The legacy
.B needs_pin
field remains true only for an actual on-screen PIN.
.PP
Each waiting connection is also listed in
.B streams
with its own target and credential kind, allowing concurrent prompts to be
completed independently.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B doubletake(1)
